d fear of heights: a factor analytic map from a large F(2) intercross of Roman rat strains</article-title><source>Brain Res Bull</source><year>2002</year><volume>57</volume><fpage>17</fpage><lpage>26</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11827733</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0361-9230(01)00632-3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ainsah</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Nabishah</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><name><surname>Osman</surname><given-names>CB</given-names></name><name><surname>Khalid</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Naloxone and vitamin E block stress-induced reduction of locomotor activity and elevation of plasma corticosterone</article-title><source>Exp Clin Endocrinol Diabetes</source><year>1999</year><volume>107</volume><fpage>462</fpage><lpage>467</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10595599</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Calvo</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Martijena</surname><given-names>ID</given-names></name><name><surname>Molina</surname><given-names>VA</given-names></name><name><surname>Volosin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Metyrapone pretreatment prevents the behavioral and neurochemical sequelae induced by stress</article-title><source>Brain Res</source><year>1998</year><volume>800</volume><fpage>227</fpage><lpage>235</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9685654</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0006-8993(98)00515-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rex</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Voigt</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Fink</surname><given